  remediation_due_date date [note: 'Due date for remediation completion']
  remediation_plan varchar [note: 'Plan to remediate non-compliance issues']
  risk_level varchar [note: 'Risk level associated with non-compliance (e.g., high, medium, low).']
  risk_rating varchar [note: 'Added to expand thin product laboratory.instrument_policy_compliance']
  updated_timestamp timestamp
  verification_evidence varchar [note: 'Evidence supporting compliance verification']
  verification_method varchar [note: 'Method used to verify compliance']
  vibe_expanded_flag boolean [note: 'Flag added by VIBE batch to expand thin product attribute set.']
  vibe_mutation_applied varchar
  vibe_mutation_marker varchar
  vibe_structure_marker varchar
  waiver_expiration_date date
  waiver_justification varchar

  Note: 'This association product represents the compliance relationship between laboratory instruments and organizational policies. It captures which policies apply to which instruments and tracks the compliance status, assessment dates, and attestation status for each instrument-policy pairing. Each record links one instrument to one policy with attributes that exist only in the context of this compliance relationship.. Existence Justification: In healthcare laboratory operations, instruments are governed by multiple organizational policies simultaneously (maintenance policy, quality control policy, safety policy, calibration policy, CLIA compliance policy), and each policy applies to multiple instruments across the laboratory. The compliance relationship itself carries operational data including compliance status, assessment dates, review schedules, and attestation status that belong to neither the instrument nor the policy alone but to the specific instrument-policy pairing.'
}

